SM(286,{"n":"Exodus 11-12.12","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Exodus 11-12.12.mp3","d":2622.2,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.44,"Okay, we'll go ahead and get started when we get started here."],[25.2,"Just a few moments we'll be picking up at the beginning of Exodus chapter 11."],[30.4,"So uh last time we went through nine of the ten plagues, and we talked about how the plagues were directed not just against Pharaoh, but against the gods of Egypt, of which they considered Pharaoh to be one."],[48.72,"But we talked about how Pharaoh's responsibility as in their minds a god king as a sort of incarnation and embodiment of Horus."],[60.12,"His job was to maintain Ma'a, to maintain justice, the correct order of things, everything functioning correctly."],[68.76,"So when there are problems like swarms of frogs, swarms of locusts, the river turning to blood, and no one can drink it."],[85.64,"And so as the plague sort of snowballed, it becomes more and more apparent that Pharaoh can't do this."],[95.02,"And we saw how Pharaoh consulted with his priests."],[97.98,"The priest's job was so sort of to advise him and tell him what they needed to do to fix things."],[103.98,"And at least with the first couple plagues, the priests were like, hey, we can do that too"],[110.18,"We could make things slightly worse."],[113.78,"But they couldn't actually fix anything."],[115.86,"They couldn't actually make it better."],[117.62,"And then we saw over the course of it, by the time we got about halfway through the plagues, the priests were like pleading with Pharaoh, like, just let them go."],[127.46,"Who cares about the Hebrews?"],[129.88,"Just you need to stop this."],[132.04,"And of course, he didn't listen to them."],[135.64,"The final plague, once we got there at the end of what we talked about last night, was the darkness that fell over the land."],[144.04,"At noontime, we talked about how that's sort of an appropriate culmination there because Ray, the sun god, was the chief god of the Egyptian pantheon at the time."],[156.96,"Not always, interestingly, but at this point at least he was."],[160.64,"And so the idea that, well, apparently he doesn't control the sunlight was sort of a very, very dramatic display."],[168.24,"And so, but we saw that even Pharaoh tried to negotiate."],[173.52,"We talked about the hubris involved in that."],[175.76,"He considered himself a god, so it's like, well, okay, the god of the Hebrews wants to tangle."],[180.88,"I'm I'm a god too."],[182.4,"We'll we will'll negotiate some kind of settlement, some kind of give and take."],[186.88,"And that wasn't happening."],[188.88,"Uh, or he would say, Oh, yeah, I'll let you go."],[191.52,"just Just you know, Moses go pray and end the pl.ague, and Moses would go do it, and then once the plague was over, he's like, Yeah, I'm not letting you go"],[199.96,"Um, so none of this has gotten through right to Pharaoh."],[207.48,"We also saw this pattern with the plagues, that the plagues would fall on the land of Egypt, except for the area in Goshen in the Nile Delta where the Israelites were."],[221.72,"So there's light there, there's darkness everywhere else."],[224.93,"There's frogs everywhere else, there's no frogs there."],[227.43,"And on and on and on."],[228.79,"Over the course of these plagues, the Egyptian food supply has been wiped out."],[233.35,"Uh their sacrificial animals have been wiped out, a lot of their people have been wiped out."],[238.15,"But Pharaoh won't relent"],[239.31,"They're now an entire situation."],[244.43,"And finally, we talked about how all of this is being done in the most powerful nation on earth at the time, as part of God revealing himself and revealing who he is."],[257.31,"Revealing who he is to the Israelites, who he's going to bring out of Egypt, revealing who he is to the Egyptians, that he's the true God, not the spirits they've been worshiping, and even revealing himself through what happens to Egypt to all the other nations of the world."],[274.83,"Because we've talked about a little bit of spoilers, we're going to see later on."],[278.43,"As the Israelites get toward other nations, they will have heard about what happened in Egypt in. Egypt, and specifically what the God of the Hebrews did"],[290.39,"And so the name of God and who he is being spread by this to all sort of to all involved parties."],[300.07,"And now as we get started tonight, we're now reaching the climax."],[304.71,"The tenth plague, the last plague, the one that God already warned Moses was going to come, but now this is going to play out."],[315.27,"So, unless we have any leftover questions, comments, excused absence notes, uh we'll go ahead and pick up in uh Exodus 11, verse 1."],[327.91,"Now the Lord said to Moses, I will bring yet one more plague on Pharaoh and on Egypt"],[333.23,"Afterward he will let you go from here."],[336.03,"When he lets you go, he will surely drive you out of here."],[340.11,"Speak now secretly in the hearing of the people, and let every one ask from his neighbor articles of silver and gold and clothing."],[348.75,"So the Lord gave the people grace in the sight of the Egyptians, and they lent to them."],[353.87,"Moreover, the man Moses was very great before the Egyptians and before Pharaoh and all his servants."],[359.79,"Keep in mind that the division with these plagues has been based on where people live."],[365.79,"And so it's not just quote unquote ethnic in modern terms, Israelites who live in Goshen in the Nile Teleg.ram"],[373.51,"So they have neighbors who are Egyptians and other from other places."],[379.01,"And so we're seeing here that the rank and file Egyptians have pattern recognition skills and have seen what's been happening."],[390.37,"They've seen what's been happening."],[399.17,"They've seen these things and understood them, and so they have a respect for Moses."],[404.07,"And a reverence for Moses and for Moses' God, and for the Israelite people and for their God, that Pharaoh not so much yet."],[415.47,"The y yetet there's not gonna be a."],[416.63,"But uh, that he doesn't share"],[418.51,"But anyway, spoilers."],[422.35,"So they're borrowing these aren't given back."],[426.43,"Yeah, I know."],[428.67,"But they're just asking for things."],[432.51,"Yeah, they're giving them to him."],[434.19,"Okay. That's a lot of respect."],[436.59,"Well, not just respect, but also you gotta you gotta think like a pagan."],[441.89,"Like they've seen all the stuff the Israelites' God has been doing."],[447.33,"And so it's like, no, no, no, no."],[449.33,"We're we're with you guys."],[451.42,"Like we're We're on your side, forget that Pharaoh guy."],[455.53,"Then Moses said to Pharaoh, thus says the Lord, about midnight I will go out into the midst of Egypt, and all the firstborn in the land of Egypt shall die."],[460.33,"the From firstborn of Pharaoh who sits on his throne, even to the firstborn of the female servant behind the handmill, and all the firstborn of the cattle."],[474.69,"So every firstborn male, from Pharaoh's firstborn son to, and then in Egyptian society, who's the lowest person?"],[484.93,"Well, a female slave who's chained up walking in circles to turn a mill."],[489.75,"That's sort of the low end of the if Pharaoh's the top, this is the bottom of the hierarchy of Egyptians."],[495.99,"Everyone's firstborn son."],[498.47,"And then this is actually a uh a Hebrew idiom when he says, and the cattle."],[505.71,"Whenever you add the cattle."],[508.05,"Egyptian, that's a way of sort of making it extreme."],[511.66,"Like even the cattle."],[512.86,"Another example of this you may be familiar with is right at the end of the book of Jonah."],[518.23,"Where God's pointing out to Jonah how silly it is that he's all upset about a vine dying that lived one day, and yet there's all these thousands of people in Nineveh who don't know their right hand from their left, and then he says, and many cattle."],[532.77,"You don't care about the people, Jonah."],[534.45,"What about the cows?"],[536.05,"The cows don't deserve to die."],[538.11,"Um, so that's that's kind of taking it to the extreme."],[542.19,"So again, Pharaoh's being told in advance."],[545.49,"This is what's going to happen."],[547.29,"And obviously, just the death of all these children is terrible as it is."],[554.41,"But you have to remember the significance of the firstborn son culturally in the ancient Near East."],[560.58,"Remember, we talked about this in Genesis."],[562.42,"We're talking about Abraham not having a son and an heir."],[566.84,"If you didn't have a firstborn son to inherit."],[570.46,"That means your family name dies, your inheritance dies."],[574.62,"Because if you have a daughter, she can't inherit."],[576.7,"Your daughter marries into some other family."],[580.14,"So with no firstborn son, your family's gone."],[583.74,"Your memory's gone from the earth."],[585.5,"Whatever you worked your whole life to achieve."],[588.84,"So this isn't just, I mean, it is a child who they love."],[589.88,"just Because these are humans like us."],[595.92,"They love their kids."],[597.41,"Not just a child who they loved, but their hope, their future."],[603.42,"For Pharaoh, this is the continuation of the dynasty."],[608.38,"This is this is this is as close to immortality as most of them understood existed."],[616.78,"Was having your name live on in your son who's your image."],[620.24,"Who carries on all of these things."],[623.24,"So losing your firstborn son is losing your hope, losing your future, watching everything you've worked your whole life to build vanish to them."],[633.72,"This isn't an inconvenience"],[636.96,"So this is this is as bad as it gets."],[641.04,"This isn't even like we're out of food, we might starve to death."],[644.32,"This is we taking your hope."],[649.41,"In the future."],[650.53,"So this is this is for the perspective of an ancient Near Easter person, this is quite literally the worst thing that could happen to you."],[661.81,"Like these fathers would rather have died themselves than lose their firstborn son."],[670.57,"'s That that's what we have to have in mind."],[673.73,"So you would think every time Moses has gone to Pharaoh before it said, This is about to happen, even when it seemed crazy, like the hail storms and the darkness at noon, it always happened exactly like he said."],[688.89,"So you would think when he goes and tells Pharaoh this."],[693.98,"Like Pharaoh would fight this would finally click."],[697.76,"This can't happen."],[698.72,"I can't let this happen to me."],[700.16,"Even if he didn't care about his people at all, he can't let it happen to his own son."],[706.12,"You'd think. Verse 6."],[708.24,"Then there shall be a great cry throughout all the land of Egypt, such as was not like it before, nor shall be like it again."],[717.24,"And this is God talking since the beginning of Egypt."],[720.52,"R rightight,? ce Sin the the beginning of world."],[723.1,"The cry that's gonna go out from people when this happens."],[726.46,"It's gonna be terrible."],[731.42,"But again, not even one of the descendants of Israel, be it man or cattle, shall a dog snarl its tongue, that you may know the Lord shall make a wide distinction between the Egyptians and Israel."],[745.18,"That's a weird translation of the Greek."],[747.42,"But it's saying, even their dogs."],[751.79,"No one among the Israelites, nothing among the Israelites is gonna is going to die."],[757.63,"And this is because."],[760.71,"Why? Because Yahweh, the God of Israel, is going to make a distinction. between the Egyptians and Israel"],[772.15,"So this is the this plague is going to be the Passover."],[776.12,"We're going to get into that more as we keep going."],[778.76,"But this is important what he says here."],[783.0,"God's purpose in this."],[785.56,"Because he hasn't been making a distinction between the Egyptians and Israel, per se."],[792.6,"He's making a distinction between where the Israelites live and the rest of Egypt."],[798.12,"So any Egyptians and anybody else who happens to live in that area has been lucky out by living where the Israelites live."],[806.6,"But now, what God is going to do through this plague is this is going to resolve who is an Egyptian and who is an Israelite."],[816.56,"Because as we've already seen and will continue to see, Israel at this point is not an ethnic unit."],[824.32,"There are people who are Israelites who have different skin colors, different what we would call ethnicities, different what we would call backgrounds, countries of origin."],[835.62,"However, we want to express that."],[838.74,"Who are Israelites?"],[841.3,"And so this is now going to be the formative experience."],[844.1,"This is where the line is going to get drawn."],[848.26,"Who's an Egyptian and who's an Israelite?"],[851.78,"And everyone who hears the anno.uncement that's about to be made is going to get to make that choice"],[859.1,"Do they want to be an Egyptian or an Israelite?"],[863.18,"And there are going to be people who are descended from Abraham by DNA."],[868.78,"Of course, they didn't know that existed then, but from our perspective, our modern perspective, are descended from Abraham, who are going to choose to become Egyptians."],[879.58,"They're going to be people who don't have an ounce of Abraham's blood in them who are going to become Israelites. here"],[887.18,"That's the distinction."],[889.1,"This firm distinction that God is about to make using this plague."],[896.22,"We're saying, and all these your servants shall come down to me and bow down to me, saying, Go from here, and all the people who follow you, after that I will go out."],[909.06,"So that's Moses talking."],[913.22,"He's saying, All of your servants are going to come bow down to me instead of you."],[921.62,"And they're going to send me out of here."],[924.51,"He says, and then I will go."],[926.91,"Then he went out from Pharaoh in great anger."],[930.11,"This is not actually Moses who's angry."],[932.35,"It's kind of unclear here."],[933.87,"It's Pharaoh. Remember, Pharaoh threatened to kill him the next time he saw him."],[938.69,"The last time Moses showed up."],[943.61,"But the Lord said to Moses, Pharaoh will not heed you, that I may multiply my signs and wonders in the land of Egypt."],[950.97,"So Moses and Aaron did all these signs and wonders in the land of Egypt before Pharaoh."],[955.45,"And the Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart, and he did not let the children of Israel depart from the land of Egypt."],[960.57,"We talked about this language last time that this is about he's not forgiving Pharaoh his sins."],[970.43,"He's not letting him off the hook anymore."],[973.87,"It's not making Pharaoh act bad."],[977.57,"It's God not forgiving, not overlooking, no longer being patient with Pharaoh."],[983.11,"He could have wiped Pharaoh out back when he was murdering all the Hebrew babies."],[986.07,"He didn't He didn't."],[991.62,"He's been patient up to this point."],[993.38,"And now, as we've seen over the course of this with the plagues, that time's at an end."],[998.42,"And now Pharaoh's going to receive the consequences."],[1001.46,"And if you think about this particular plague and this particular consequence, what initiated all this at the beginning of the book of Exodus?"],[1012.98,"Killing the firstborn Hebrews."],[1014.5,"Pharaoh or the murder of the Hebrew baby boys."],[1020.9,"And when the midwives wouldn't do it, he brought in all the Egyptian people, made it open season."],[1026.74,"They were drowning them in the river."],[1029.5,"They were killing Hebrew children."],[1033.74,"So this particular consequence is kind of rough justice."],[1039.12,"This is what's going to befall the people who choose to be Egyptians now is going to be what they did to God's people."],[1048.96,"They're going to be on the receiving end now."],[1051.36,"Chapter 12. Now the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt, saying, This month shall be your beginning of months."],[1059.76,"It shall be the first month of the year for you."],[1064.24,"Speak to all the congregation of the children of Israel, saying, On the tenth day of this month, every man shall take for himself a lamb, according to the family households, a lamb for each home."],[1074.48,"Let's hit pause here for a second"],[1079.64,"Anything strike you as odd?"],[1083.4,"There might be a couple of things."],[1084.84,"Oh little odd."],[1085.96,"Yeah. Don't you think it's odd that before this thing has actually happened, Moses is telling them how they're going to commemorate it every year?"],[1102.68,"And he's doing that before it happens."],[1106.52,"Well, he knows it's going to happen."],[1108.86,"But he's instructing them, hey, this thing's going to happen tonight."],[1113.26,"And in the future, every year, on this day, here's what we're. gonna do"],[1121.94,"Seems like your focus would be on, hey guys, get ready to leave Egypt."],[1125.32,"You know, like sort of yeah, and then once you're out, then we can talk about, hey, we're gonna commemorate every year what God just did."],[1132.85,"Like that would be the more natural, the more natural way to do it."],[1139.73,"Now, let me throw this out."],[1141.25,"Does this remind you of anything in the New Testament?"],[1146.13,"Oh, Christ at the Last Supper?"],[1148.5,"So Christ dies when?"],[1151.38,"Do this in a reverse?"],[1152.42,"The Passover. Uh-huh."],[1154.99,"And right before his death happens."],[1159.39,"The Eucharist. He institutes the Eucharist."],[1161.39,"His body hadn't been broken yet"],[1161.75,"He says, This is my body broken for you."],[1169.19,"This is my blood of the new covenant shed for you."],[1171.75,"It hadn't been shed yet."],[1175.67,"That was about to happen."],[1181.03,"Some of our Protestant friends try to argue from that that that's why it can't really be his body and blood, because it's beforehand."],[1187.59,"John chapter 6."],[1188.71,"Have you read the Torah?"],[1189.67,"But anyway, it's following the same pattern."],[1194.79,"It's following the same pattern."],[1200.17,"Because this thing that's about to happen, and it's important they know even before. it happens, that this isn't a one-time thing"],[1212.05,"The event there that's about to happen, what's about to happen, is something of cosmic and eternal importance."],[1220.29,"And it's something that's going to have this ongoing effect and ongoing participation."],[1228.55,"Not just in their life from year to year, but their children, their children's children, on into the future."],[1237.04,"So it's a way of indicating the supreme importance of the event."],[1243.04,"That going into it, the people know."],[1246.62,"This is something of ongoing. permanent significance that's about to happen"],[1257.46,"Now notice also, that God tells the Wells, this will be the first month for you."],[1268.97,"This will be the first month for you."],[1270.73,"We're gonna get into more feasts and stuff as we keep going through the twelve month."],[1278.09,"But Rosh Hashanah, which is the head of the year or the first of the year, new year, feast of trumpets, that's gonna be another feast."],[1286.33,"It's gonna be in at a completely different time."],[1289.53,"Usually about six months later."],[1291.69,"So what's going on with that?"],[1293.17,"How can this be the first of months and that be the first day of the year?"],[1297.97,"It's just the most important feast."],[1300.05,"No. There's two overlapping calendars described in the Torah."],[1306.45,"So the calendar that they already have before this is the agricultural calendar that they share with most ancient Near Eastern countries."],[1316.61,"Which the year begins in September, because it's based on the agricultural cycle."],[1322.61,"And so Israel is going to have fixed feasts that are on the same day of the same month every year that are on that agricultural calendar."],[1334.61,"And then there's gonna be this overlay."],[1337.25,"That's gonna be based on Passover"],[1338.43,"That's overlaid over the top of that."],[1344.11,"And it's later going to include Shavot, which we call Pentecost, 50 days after the Passover."],[1352.67,"That event hasn't happened yet."],[1354.19,"We'll get there here in Exodus."],[1356.64,"And those are going to sort of float over the top of the regular yearly calendar."],[1363.2,"Does that sound familiar to anybody?"],[1365.52,"That's exactly how the Christian calendar works."],[1371.2,"Because guess where we got it?"],[1373.28,"From that scriptures."],[1376.3,"So we also have Pasca is just the Greek word for. Passover"],[1384.9,"So we also have Passover Pentecost."],[1388.12,"We have feasts that are based on the relationship to the Passover that floats over the top of our regular calendar, our ecclesiastical new year."],[1399.72,"Our new year is technically September 1st."],[1403.48,"It's the same, and we still follow."],[1408.2,"But that pattern is here being established in the Torah"],[1415.26,"They already had the agricultural calendar."],[1417.34,"They're already farmers."],[1419.2,"But this new overlay based on Passover, that's what's getting added here."],[1422.88,"'s what's getting added here. That"],[1428.2,"It's interesting because it's kind of like the in a way, it's kind of like the two firmaments."],[1433.56,"Like there's a weird kind of lavish and shape."],[1439.4,"Yeah, the movement of the stars compared to the planets and the sun and the moon."],[1443.4,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[1445.08,"And they're working on a lunar calendar, and that's why the dating of Passover is going to be based on the phases of the moon."],[1451.32,"They date it the same way we do."],[1453.96,"I'm not going to go into it all now, but let's just say everybody Jewish and everybody Christian actually dates Passover the same way."],[1462.36,"Exact same way."],[1463.4,"We just disagree about when the moon is full."],[1467.96,"That's literally the difference."],[1469.24,"But I'm not going to go into all that right now"],[1469.76,"We disagree about when the mood is full."],[1474.24,"But so that that overlay is what's being established here."],[1479.44,"And so on the tenth day of the month, every man is going to take a lamb for his household."],[1488.24,"One lamb per household."],[1492.4,"Verse 4 If there be too few in a household, let him and his neighbor next to his house take it according to the number of souls."],[1500.64,"He will make his count in lambs according to the needs of each one."],[1505.2,"What is that?"],[1506.0,"That's a convoluted way of saying if you've got a really small family and you can't eat a whole lamb, then get together with another small family and share one."],[1513.6,"Your lamb shall be without blemish, a male of the first year, you shall take it from the sheep or the kids."],[1519.32,"Then you shall keep it until the fourteenth day of the same month, and the whole assembly of the congregation of Israel shall kill it at twilight."],[1528.76,"Then they shall take some of the blood and put it on the two doorposts and on the lintel of the houses where they eat it."],[1535.32,"They shall eat the flesh on that night roasted in fire, with unleavened bread and bitter herbs."],[1540.6,"They shall eat it."],[1542.28,"Do not eat it raw, nor boiled it all with water, but roasted in fire, its head with its legs and its entrails."],[1549.48,"You shall let none of it remain until morning, nor shall you break a bone of it, and what remains of it until morning you shall burn with fire."],[1556.68,"So anything left the next morning, you burn it up."],[1559.64,"Okay Thus you shall eat it with a belt on."],[1563.52,"Well, we'll pause there."],[1564.4,"We'll pause there."],[1566.48,"So they're eating this lamb."],[1569.6,"They're putting the blood to mark to mark the doorposts."],[1574.72,"So we'll start with marking the doorposts."],[1578.0,"What's the point of this with the lamb's blood?"],[1581.6,"This is how the distinction is being made between Israel and Egypt."],[1587.04,"So it doesn't matter who your dad is, or your grandfather."],[1592.73,"If you do this and you put the blood on your doorpost, you're an Israelite."],[1598.97,"If you don't, you're now an Egyptian."],[1602.97,"So this is the distinction"],[1605.25,"This is in the first place, in the first instance, when it happens the first time, this is what decides who's an Israelite and who's not."],[1613.97,"But that's gonna be true on an ongoing basis."],[1618.13,"It's gonna be true on an ongoing basis."],[1621.49,"What someone will do, we'll see this as we keep going in the Torah when we get into Leviticus."],[1627.17,"If someone wants to become an Israelite, if they're male, they get circumcised and they eat the Passover."],[1637.17,"That's what makes you an Israelite."],[1640.37,"And if, from the perspective of ancient Israel and later Judaism, if you stop celebrating the Passover, you stop being an Israelite."],[1653.85,"I've been at Passover satyrs in Jewish homes, and you know they actually eat these various things."],[1662.17,"Yeah. And you know, the bitter herbs are horseradit."],[1665.53,"Yeah. Yeah. And each thing, it's it's us, it's now."],[1669.77,"Yeah. It's this time."],[1671.13,"And we'll get into that here in a little bit."],[1672.57,"Yeah. So that's where the distinction is made."],[1677.69,"And by the way, this also is true in the Orthodox Church."],[1683.29,"This is cannot, what do you need to do to be a Christian?"],[1685.85,"You have to be baptized, you have to receive the Eucharist."],[1690.57,"And if you look at the canons, the bare minimum. to stay an Orthodox Christian is that you have to receive the Eucharist on Pasca, on the Passover"],[1701.81,"You have to receive it on Passover."],[1703.73,"If you go a whole year without receiving the Eucharist, you are no longer an Orthodox Christian."],[1708.93,"You are considered to be lapsed."],[1711.01,"And there's actually a service to reconcile you to the church."],[1715.25,"That happens. It's kind of a nice service."],[1717.73,"And I wish we would use it more."],[1719.81,"But people for some reason don't want to use it."],[1722.77,"But it's actually very beautiful about, you know, returning to God."],[1726.93,"And there are people for whom that's a real experience."],[1730.31,"If you're coming back to church after a long time, especially after more than a year, I would think you would want those prayers."],[1736.77,"And you'd have that sense."],[1738.05,"It's prayers Whatever I was off doing, now I'm right, I'm returning to God."],[1742.65,"We don't baptize people again or anything."],[1747.61,"Asking God to strengthen them."],[1749.79,"Keep them from wandering off again."],[1753.95,"But yeah, so it's the same."],[1756.51,"We have the same thing."],[1757.95,"But so this the blood on the doorpost is making this distinction."],[1761.63,"Now I have to say something about the lamb."],[1763.63,"And I have to say something about the lamb."],[1766.19,"Not to pick on them, but we need to straighten this out for our Protestant friends."],[1774.39,"Because I have heard very, very well-educated people with PhDs who are Bible scholars in the Protestant world read this and say, well, obviously, this is substitutionary atonement."],[1792.07,"Obviously, they are killing the lamb instead of their child getting killed."],[1799.29,"So the lamb is like a substitute for their for their firstborn son."],[1807.13,"Literally say it's obvious."],[1809.37,"Like it's obvious, like it's right there."],[1813.45,"Let me explain why it's not obvious, if anyone here thinks it's obvious."],[1818.17,"So, number one, what if you don't have a firstborn son?"],[1824.33,"What if you're a guy who has an older brother and you only have daughters?"],[1827.73,"Do you not have to do it?"],[1832.5,"I mean, your older brother has to, because he's the firstborn."],[1835.06,"But if you're not, and you just have daughters, do you not have to do it?"],[1843.06,"And if it's we're substituting a lamb for a for a child."],[1848.08,"What if you're the firstborn son of a firstborn son of a firstborn son?"],[1854.48,"So in your household, there's three firstborn sons."],[1857.12,"Oh, wait, there's only one lamb."],[1859.44,"You don't do three lambs."],[1861.28,"Or if you share a lamb, you do one lamb."],[1864.02,"So you have a firstborn son, but you only have one kid, and your neighbor has a firstborn son and they only have one kid, so the two of you share a lamb."],[1870.66,"lamb Now you got one and two kids."],[1876.24,"So it's built into the instructions here that it is not one lamb per firstborn son."],[1882.88,"So since it is not apportioned one lamb per firstborn son, it cannot be substitution."],[1888.4,"That cannot be how this works."],[1893.22,"It just can't."],[1894.9,"It's kind of obvious."],[1896.26,"But um but I'm not I'm not saying that to pick on people."],[1900.5,"It's just, and it's that people have just been taught this."],[1903.78,"Whenever someone points at the Bible or refers to the Bible and says, W,ell it's obvious."],[1909.86,"That's a sure sign that they're just going on something they've been taught."],[1914.9,"That's what makes it obvious"],[1915.34,"Because that's what makes things obvious."],[1921.34,"Is that that's what you've been taught all your life, so when you look at it, that's what you see."],[1926.62,"And so that's just it's not here."],[1930.3,"It's not here."],[1931.18,"And I would add to that, I would add to that, why would God want to kill the firstborn sons of the Israelites in the first place?"],[1941.98,"For what reason?"],[1945.43,"The firstborn sons of the Egyptians, that's this balancing the skills of justice thing, because they murdered the sons of the Israelites."],[1954.07,"Why would God want to murder more of his people?"],[1958.79,"Unless they appease him with the lamb."],[1959.99,"That doesn't make sense"],[1965.19,"So you have to add all these things into the text that either contradict what's there or just kind of don't make sense in order to get this substitution idea in."],[1976.79,"So let's just leave it out."],[1980.55,"So what about the line, though, a male of the first year?"],[1983.51,"Like there must be some, you're supposed to get some connection there."],[1987.48,"Well, though, the lamb, well, your firstborn son might be a lot more than a year old, but um, so it's that it's an adult, but it's not an old sheep."],[1998.78,"Because the idea here is it's supposed to be you you give God your best."],[2001.74,"We're gonna see that all through the sacrificial rules."],[2004.35,"You don't go and find some old sheep, some sheep with a broken leg that you'd have to put down anyway, and say, Oh, okay, well, we're offering this one to God."],[2012.65,"Um that's what the one year is."],[2014.97,"So it's it's an adult, but it's not like old."],[2017.93,"It's like prime animal."],[2022.09,"And males, you you usually have fewer males around than females when you're herding animals."],[2030.93,"So you have a few males around to breed with all the females."],[2035.39,"And so the males are sort of prized."],[2037.72,"It's the difference between sacrificing a bull and sacrificing a cow."],[2041.74,"The bull, if it's a bull that'ss actively producing offspring is sort of more prized than the cow."],[2052.2,"For that reason."],[2053.48,"So that's why it's a male lamb that age."],[2057.96,"So the idea is this is this would be the top one you have, the one you'd least want to part with."],[2064.54,"Of your of your sheep."],[2066.46,"God gets the best, not the leftovers."],[2070.88,"And even later on when we look at the sacrifices in Leviticus, and there's all these rules about cutting this part and that part, the fatty part over the kidneys, and right all this."],[2081.6,"The idea behind all that is that God gets the best parts."],[2085.12,"God gets the parts that you'd want to take to eat yourself if you could choose."],[2089.72,"Those go to God, you get the other parts."],[2095.24,"Yes, sir. This, so like knowing that the sacrificial system comes in Leviticus, this isn't a sacrifice to God."],[2104.17,"So there is not described here an actual offering to God of any part of the lamb."],[2110.57,"In fact, you're supposed to eat the whole thing."],[2113.35,"The family is supposed to eat the whole thing."],[2115.69,"But yeah, there's no altar involved."],[2120.09,"Um, would this have been viewed as a sacrifice, like a sacrificial would it have been like viewed as like a meal with God, or would it have been viewed as just like God's provision or is that even the wrong? kind of context"],[2133.01,"Yeah, I think that's kind of the wrong context."],[2135.25,"I think it's a slightly different thing."],[2138.77,"The word that they use for slaughtering the animal is the same word that they use for killing a sacrifice."],[2146.05,"But there's just not a piece offered to God."],[2149.27,"Which is sacrifices later, either the whole thing, you do a whole burnt offering and the whole thing goes to God, or some part of the best parts."],[2158.87,"It's more like an issue."],[2161.19,"So this is more uh this is more aimed at the identity of the people and the family unit."],[2174.25,"And notice this is not an individual thing."],[2176.01,"al. More like a memori feast as opposed to"],[2177.18,"It's a community."],[2178.14,"This is done by the household."],[2183.42,"So it's not I I am an Israelite individually."],[2187.1,"It's my household is an Israelite household."],[2191.34,"And because I belong to it, I'm an Israelite."],[2196.46,"Um and this is directly related to what I tell people all the time."],[2200.8,"You don't join the Orthodox Church."],[2203.92,"You join an Orthodox Church, you join a community, a family, and then because you're part of that Orthodox Church, that community, that family, you're part of the Orthodox Church."],[2218.77,"Um it's the same kind of dynamic here."],[2221.79,"You're part of a household, a family that is an Israelite, household and family."],[2228.27,"That makes you part of that makes you an Israelite, in the broad, in the broad sense."],[2235.73,"Verse 11, thus you shall eat it, with a belt on your waist, your sandals on your feet, and your staff in your hand, you shall eat it in haste."],[2244.29,"It is the Lord's pasca."],[2246.61,"They didn't translate it, but pasca is the Greek word for Passover."],[2253.81,"For I will pass through the land of Egypt on that night, and will strike all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both man and beast."],[2260.77,"Against all the gods of Egypt, I will execute vengeance."],[2263.65,"I am the Lord."],[2264.29,"Notice that phrasing"],[2269.05,"Against all the gods of Egypt, I will take vengeance."],[2274.17,"Let me submit to you the gods of Egypt here, who he's been attacking with the plagues and everything, are not fictional characters."],[2283.22,"That would not be impressive."],[2286.98,"Saying that God can beat up Batman is not impressive."],[2291.22,"He's a fictional character."],[2293.62,"I can beat up fictional characters."],[2300.23,"This is talking about the actual demonic spirits that the Egyptians have been worshiping that they've been following."],[2308.71,"Why is God taking vengeance on them?"],[2312.87,"Because they're the ones who led the Egyptians down the path that led to them murdering the Hebrew children."],[2321.11,"They're the ones that led them to the sin and wickedness."],[2326.61,"That they're now being judged for."],[2337.65,"And so they're the ones who received the vengeance."],[2341.25,"What does that also mean, though?"],[2343.57,"Who's God's enemy?"],[2344.93,"God's enemy is not any of the humans involved here."],[2349.89,"It's not the Egyptian people."],[2354.25,"It's not even Pharaoh qua human."],[2358.17,"Pharaoh qua pretensions to godhood, yes, but just as the human guy, the human male, who happened to be Pharaoh at the time."],[2368.46,"Was not, as a human, God's enemy."],[2372.94,"But maybe God's enemy was his pretensions to Godhood."],[2377.04,"The God who Pharaoh was supposed to be."],[2379.92,"That's God's enemy."],[2383.68,"And the enemy of his people."],[2386.24,"Do you think that's why we don't have like a name for Pharaoh?"],[2389.28,"I think it's part of it."],[2391.52,"I think it's probably part of it."],[2393.93,"That these are not. the actual enemy"],[2397.81,"It's the spirits, the demonic powers, the sin that lies behind these people that has seduced these people."],[2403.57,"The idea of Pharaoh, which includes his godhead."],[2409.77,"Pharaoh's a throne."],[2411.27,"Yeah. And so this is this is why this is important and why it's important that it comes here in terms of this distinction being drawn through between Egyptians and Israelites."],[2425.91,"Because it's kind of obvious to us how the Israelites are about to be set free."],[2431.59,"They're slaves. They're not going to be slaves anymore."],[2434.81,"That's just straight manumission."],[2436.65,"You were slaves, now you're not slaves."],[2440.29,"But what about the people who had been Egyptians?"],[2447.41,"Who, because of what they've seen unfold in these last nine plagues, and what they've seen of Moses and what they've seen of the Israelites, decide to kill the lamb, mark their door, and eat it and become Israelites."],[2461.65,"They weren't necessarily slaves, but they're also being set free."],[2475.61,"They're being set free from the slavery to sin and wickedness, that had entrapped them."],[2483.34,"So when St"],[2486.1,"Paul, for example, or the gospel writers in the New Testament, use that language about the Passover when Christ dies and rises again, about us being set free from slavery to sin."],[2498.02,"That's not just an analogy to the Israelites being set free from Egypt."],[2504.5,"That's what happened then, too."],[2509.86,"That's what happened then too."],[2512.82,"In a very literal sense."],[2514.34,"These people are very literally enslaved by their passions, by trying to feed the desires of their flesh."],[2523.38,"And God is going to bring a bunch of them, even though they were quote unquote Gentiles."],[2529.98,"He's going to bring a bunch of them, make them part of Israel, give them the Torah, give them a way to live where they won't fall prey to those things again."],[2545.98,"And so that's going to become especially important to, for example, St."],[2550.46,"Paul, who spent a lot of time studying the Torah, in understanding what he needed to say to the Gentiles again, the non-Jewish people who he was talking to about Jesus as the Messiah."],[2566.06,"The freedom that was being offered them."],[2567.02,"that was being offered them The new way of life to."],[2572.24,"It was the same thing that gets offered. to the to the Egyptians here"],[2577.8,"And whoever else, you know, the Libyans from Put, the Nubians, the other people from Levant Hittites."],[2584.62,"Whoever, whoever is here, has the opportunity now to become an Israelite, to become one of God's people, and to be set free from the actual enemies of both God and humans."],[2599.78,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2607.14,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2612.5,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.44,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: nine plagues","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>Exodus 11</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Last time: nine of ten plagues - directed not just at Pharaoh but at the <b>gods of Egypt</b>, Pharaoh considered one</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh = <b>god-king</b>, incarnation of <b>Horus</b> - job: maintain <b>Ma'at</b> = justice, correct order, everything functioning</li><li class=\"d1\">frogs, locusts, river to blood → plague <b>snowballs</b>, Pharaoh clearly <b>can't</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Priests</b> advise how to fix things</li><li class=\"d1\">first plagues: \"we can do that too\" - could only make it <b>slightly worse</b></li><li class=\"d1\">by halfway: <b>pleading</b> with Pharaoh - \"just let them go... who cares about the Hebrews?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Ninth plague: darkness at <b>noon</b> - <b>Ra</b>, chief god at this point (not always)</li></ul>"},{"t":168.24,"lv":3,"h":"Recap: negotiation and Goshen","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh tried to <b>negotiate</b> - <b>hubris</b>: \"I'm a god too, we'll work out a settlement\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'll let you go - Moses go pray\" → plague ends → \"not letting you go\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern: plagues fall on Egypt <b>except Goshen</b>, Nile Delta</li><li class=\"d1\">light there, darkness elsewhere; frogs elsewhere</li><li class=\"d0\">Egypt's <b>food supply</b>, <b>sacrificial animals</b>, many <b>people</b> wiped out - Pharaoh won't relent</li><li class=\"d0\">All in the <b>most powerful nation</b>: God <b>revealing who he is</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to <b>Israelites</b>, to <b>Egyptians</b> (true God, not the spirits), to <b>other nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spoiler: later nations will have <b>heard what the God of the Hebrews did</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now the <b>climax</b> - tenth plague, already warned</li></ul>"},{"t":327.91,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 11:1-3 - Silver and gold from the Egyptians","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"One more plague\" → afterward he'll let you go - \"<b>surely drive you out</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Speak secretly to people: each <b>ask his neighbor</b> for silver, gold, clothing</li><li class=\"d0\">Lord gave the people <b>grace in the sight of the Egyptians</b>; Moses <b>very great</b> before Egyptians and Pharaoh's servants</li><li class=\"d0\">Division based on <b>where people live</b> - not \"ethnic\" in modern terms</li><li class=\"d1\">Israelites in Goshen have <b>Egyptian neighbors</b> and others</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rank-and-file Egyptians</b> have <b>pattern recognition</b> - they've seen it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>respect, reverence</b> for Moses, Moses' God, Israelites - Pharaoh doesn't share it \"yet\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not given back - Q: they're just asking? → they <b>give</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"think like a pagan\": seen what the Israelites' God is doing → \"<b>we're with you guys</b>, forget that Pharaoh guy\"</li></ul>"},{"t":455.53,"lv":2,"h":"11:4-5 - Death of the firstborn announced","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses to Pharaoh: <b>about midnight</b> I go out into Egypt - <b>all firstborn die</b></li><li class=\"d1\">from Pharaoh's firstborn on the throne to the <b>female servant behind the handmill</b></li><li class=\"d1\">lowest of Egyptian hierarchy: slave <b>chained, walking in circles</b> to turn a mill</li><li class=\"d1\">everyone's firstborn <b>son</b>; and the <b>firstborn of the cattle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"And the cattle\" = <b>Hebrew idiom</b>, makes it <b>extreme</b></li><li class=\"d1\">end of <b>Jonah</b>: vine that lived one day; thousands who don't know right from left, \"<b>and many cattle</b>\" - \"what about the cows?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh being told <b>in advance</b></li></ul>"},{"t":547.29,"lv":3,"h":"Why the firstborn son matters","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Culturally in the <b>ancient Near East</b> - recall <b>Genesis</b>: Abraham with no son and heir</li><li class=\"d1\">no firstborn son → <b>family name dies</b>, inheritance dies</li><li class=\"d1\">daughter can't inherit - <b>marries into another family</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"your memory's gone from the earth\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just a child they love (\"humans like us\") - their <b>hope, their future</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh: <b>continuation of the dynasty</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>as close to immortality</b> as most understood - name lives on in son, <b>your image</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"This isn't an inconvenience\" - not \"we might starve\" - <b>we're taking your hope</b></li><li class=\"d1\">literally <b>the worst thing</b> for an ancient Near Easterner - fathers would rather <b>die themselves</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Every earlier warning, even crazy (hail, darkness at noon), came true exactly</li><li class=\"d1\">you'd think this would <b>finally click</b> - \"can't let it happen to his own son\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"You'd think\"</li></ul>"},{"t":706.12,"lv":2,"h":"11:6-7 - Great cry; a distinction","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v6: <b>great cry</b> through all Egypt - <b>never before, never again</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God speaking; \"since the beginning of the world\"</li><li class=\"d0\">v7: not one descendant of Israel, <b>man or cattle</b> - \"<b>a dog snarl its tongue</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"weird translation of the Greek\" - even their <b>dogs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nothing among Israelites dies → Lord makes a <b>wide distinction</b> between Egyptians and Israel</li><li class=\"d0\">This plague = the <b>Passover</b> - more as we go</li></ul>"},{"t":783.0,"lv":3,"h":"Who is an Egyptian, who an Israelite?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Until now distinction = <b>where Israelites live</b> - anyone living there \"lucked out\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now the plague <b>resolves who is Egyptian and who is Israelite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israel at this point <b>not an ethnic unit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israelites of different <b>skin colors, ethnicities, countries of origin</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Formative experience</b> - where the line gets drawn</li><li class=\"d1\">everyone who hears the announcement <b>chooses</b>: Egyptian or Israelite?</li><li class=\"d0\">Some <b>descended from Abraham by DNA</b> will choose to become <b>Egyptians</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some with <b>not an ounce of Abraham's blood</b> will become <b>Israelites</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"That's the distinction\"</li></ul>"},{"t":896.22,"lv":2,"h":"11:8-10 - Moses leaves; hardening","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v8: <b>all your servants</b> will bow to <b>me</b> - \"go from here\"; \"after that I will go out\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses \"went out from Pharaoh in great anger\" - actually <b>Pharaoh's</b> anger</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh had threatened to <b>kill him</b> next time he saw him</li><li class=\"d0\">Lord: Pharaoh won't heed → <b>multiply my signs and wonders</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart</b> - as last time: <b>not forgiving</b> his sins, not letting him off the hook</li><li class=\"d1\">not <b>making</b> him act bad - God no longer <b>patient</b></li><li class=\"d1\">could have wiped him out when he was <b>murdering Hebrew babies</b> - didn't</li><li class=\"d1\">patience at an end → <b>consequences</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rough justice: what started it all = <b>killing Hebrew baby boys</b></li><li class=\"d1\">midwives wouldn't → <b>open season</b>, drowned in the river</li><li class=\"d1\">those who <b>choose to be Egyptians</b> receive what they did to God's people</li></ul>"},{"t":1051.36,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 12:1-4 - First month; the lamb","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 12</b> - \"This month your <b>beginning of months</b>\" - first month of the year</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tenth day</b>: every man takes a <b>lamb</b> per household</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Let's hit pause - anything strike you as odd?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">before it happens Moses is telling them <b>how to commemorate it every year</b></li><li class=\"d1\">you'd expect \"get ready to leave Egypt\" - commemoration <b>after</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1139.73,"lv":3,"h":"Parallel: the Last Supper","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">NT parallel? <b>Christ at the Last Supper</b></li><li class=\"d1\">dies at <b>Passover</b>; <b>institutes the Eucharist</b> before death</li><li class=\"d1\">\"This is my body <b>broken</b> for you\" - not yet broken; blood of new covenant <b>shed</b> - not yet shed</li><li class=\"d0\">Protestants argue: can't really be body and blood because beforehand → \"<b>John 6</b>. Have you read the Torah?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same <b>pattern</b>: it's important they know even before - <b>not a one-time thing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">event of <b>cosmic and eternal importance</b>, ongoing participation</li><li class=\"d1\">children, children's children, into the future</li><li class=\"d1\">signals the <b>supreme importance</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1257.46,"lv":3,"h":"Two overlapping calendars","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"First month for you\" - but <b>Rosh Hashanah</b> (head of year, <b>Feast of Trumpets</b>) ~<b>six months</b> later - how both?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two overlapping calendars</b> in the Torah</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>agricultural calendar</b> shared with the ancient Near East - year begins in <b>September</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fixed feasts same day, same month</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>overlay based on Passover</b> - later <b>Shavuot</b> = <b>Pentecost</b>, 50 days after</li><li class=\"d1\">floats over the regular year</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Exactly how the <b>Christian calendar</b> works\" - got it from Scriptures</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>Pascha</i> = Greek for Passover; <b>Passover, Pentecost</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ecclesiastical new year technically <b>September 1</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: like the <b>two firmaments</b>? (stars vs. planets, sun, moon)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>lunar</b> calendar - Passover dated by <b>phases of the moon</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jews and Christians date it the <b>same way</b> - \"we just disagree about when the moon is full\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1479.44,"lv":2,"h":"12:3-10 - Lamb rules","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Tenth day: <b>one lamb per household</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v4: too few → share with <b>neighbor</b> by number of souls - \"get together with another small family\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Without blemish</b>, <b>male of the first year</b>, from sheep or kids</li><li class=\"d0\">Keep until <b>14th day</b>; whole assembly kills it at <b>twilight</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Blood</b> on <b>two doorposts and the lintel</b> of houses where they eat it</li><li class=\"d0\">Eat that night <b>roasted in fire</b>, <b>unleavened bread, bitter herbs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not raw, not boiled; head, legs, entrails</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>None remains until morning</b>; <b>no bone broken</b>; leftovers <b>burned</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v11 begins: \"eat it with a belt on\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1566.48,"lv":3,"h":"Blood on the doorpost: Israelite or not","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Point of the blood = <b>how the distinction is made</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't matter who your dad or grandfather is</li><li class=\"d1\">put blood on doorpost → <b>Israelite</b>; don't → <b>Egyptian</b></li><li class=\"d0\">First instance decides; also <b>ongoing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">later (<b>Leviticus</b>): male wanting to become Israelite → <b>circumcised + eats the Passover</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ancient Israel and Judaism: <b>stop celebrating Passover, stop being Israelite</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Passover seders in Jewish homes: bitter herbs = <b>horseradish</b>; \"it's now, this time\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same in the <b>Orthodox Church</b>: baptized + <b>Eucharist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">canons' bare minimum: receive the Eucharist <b>on Pascha</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a whole year without → <b>lapsed</b>; <b>service to reconcile</b> you - \"very beautiful... I wish we'd use it more\"</li><li class=\"d1\">prayers: returning to God, strengthen, keep from wandering; <b>no rebaptism</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1757.95,"lv":2,"h":"Not substitution: against the Protestant reading","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Say something about the lamb\" - <b>well-educated Protestant PhDs</b>: \"obviously <b>substitutionary atonement</b>\" - lamb dies instead of firstborn</li><li class=\"d0\">Why it's not obvious</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no firstborn son</b>? only daughters, younger brother - do you not do it?</li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn of firstborn of firstborn - three firstborn sons, <b>one lamb</b></li><li class=\"d1\">two families share a lamb: <b>two kids, one lamb</b></li><li class=\"d1\">instructions <b>not one lamb per firstborn</b> → can't be substitution</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Whenever someone says 'it's <b>obvious</b>' - sure sign they're going on what they've been <b>taught</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why would God kill the <b>Israelites' firstborn</b> in the first place?</li><li class=\"d1\">Egyptians' = <b>scales of justice</b> for murdering Israelite sons</li><li class=\"d1\">\"why murder more of his people - unless they <b>appease</b> him with a lamb?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">have to add things that <b>contradict or don't make sense</b> - \"let's leave it out\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1980.55,"lv":3,"h":"Male of the first year: God gets the best","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Male of the first year\" - connection?</li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn son may be older - lamb = <b>adult but not old</b>, <b>prime</b></li><li class=\"d1\">give God your <b>best</b> - not an old sheep with a <b>broken leg</b> you'd have to put down anyway</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Males</b> prized: fewer than females; a few breed with all the females</li><li class=\"d1\">bull producing offspring more prized than a cow</li><li class=\"d0\">The one you'd <b>least want to part with</b> - \"God gets the best, not the leftovers\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Leviticus</b>: fatty part over the kidneys etc. - God gets the <b>best parts</b>, the ones you'd choose to eat</li></ul>"},{"t":2095.24,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: Is this a sacrifice?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: sacrificial system comes in <b>Leviticus</b> - not a sacrifice to God? meal with God? God's provision?</li><li class=\"d0\">No <b>altar</b>; <b>no piece offered to God</b> - <b>family eats the whole thing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Wrong context\" - same <b>word</b> as for killing a sacrifice</li><li class=\"d1\">later: whole <b>burnt offering</b>, or best parts to God</li><li class=\"d0\">More aimed at <b>identity of the people and family unit</b> - more like a <b>memorial feast</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not individual: done by the <b>household</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"my household is an Israelite household; because I belong to it, I'm an Israelite\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Parallel: \"you don't join <b>the</b> Orthodox Church, you join <b>an</b> Orthodox Church\" - community, family</li><li class=\"d1\">being part of that makes you part of the Church; same dynamic</li></ul>"},{"t":2235.73,"lv":2,"h":"12:11-12 - Eaten in haste; vengeance on the gods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v11: <b>belt on waist, sandals on feet, staff in hand</b>, in haste</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"It is the Lord's <i>pascha</i>\"</b> - untranslated; Greek for Passover</li><li class=\"d0\">v12: pass through Egypt that night, strike all firstborn, man and beast</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"Against all the gods of Egypt I will execute vengeance\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>fictional characters</b> - \"God can beat up Batman is not impressive\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>actual demonic spirits</b> the Egyptians worshiped</li><li class=\"d1\">they <b>led Egyptians</b> down the path to murdering Hebrew children - sin now judged</li><li class=\"d0\">God's enemy: not the <b>Egyptian people</b>, not <b>Pharaoh qua human</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Pharaoh qua pretensions to godhood</b> - the god he was supposed to be</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: why no <b>name for Pharaoh</b>? → part of it: not the actual enemy</li><li class=\"d1\">spirits, demonic powers, <b>sin</b> behind; \"the idea of Pharaoh\" - <b>a throne</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2411.27,"lv":3,"h":"Set free: Egyptians who become Israelites","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Importance: obvious that <b>Israelites</b> are set free - slaves, <b>straight manumission</b></li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>former Egyptians</b> who, from nine plagues, <b>kill the lamb, mark the door, eat it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not necessarily slaves - also <b>set free</b>: from <b>slavery to sin and wickedness</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul</b>, gospel writers: Passover language - Christ dies and rises → free from slavery to sin</li><li class=\"d1\">not just <b>analogy</b> to Israel leaving Egypt - <b>that's what happened then too</b>, literally</li><li class=\"d1\">enslaved by <b>passions</b>, feeding desires of the flesh</li><li class=\"d0\">God brings many <b>\"Gentiles\"</b> into Israel, gives the <b>Torah</b> - a way of life so they don't fall prey again</li><li class=\"d0\">Matters for <b>Paul</b>: studied Torah, understanding what to tell <b>Gentiles</b> about Jesus as Messiah</li><li class=\"d1\">same freedom, new way of life offered <b>to the Egyptians here</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Whoever else - <b>Libyans from Put, Nubians, Levant, Hittites</b> - chance to become an Israelite</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>set free from the actual enemies</b> of God and humans</li></ul>"}]});
